00:11:18.515 --> 00:11:19.699
very carefully.

00:11:19.699 --> 00:11:22.044
I think it comes down to

00:11:22.044 --> 00:11:26.478
realizing that people wanna
be surgical and execution

00:11:26.478 --> 00:11:31.030
oriented on your site, and
you as a marketing engine

00:11:31.030 --> 00:11:33.979
need to be great at creating discovery

00:11:33.979 --> 00:11:36.068
across the whole web, and then funneling

00:11:36.068 --> 00:11:39.176
it to surgical execution on your site.

00:11:39.176 --> 00:11:40.707
That was tremendous advice.

00:11:41.780 --> 00:11:44.288
- [Voiceover] Andrew asks,
"if you were to tragically die

00:11:44.288 --> 00:11:47.120
today, how well would
VaynerMedia do in the long term

00:11:47.120 --> 00:11:48.351
without it's CEO?

00:11:48.351 --> 00:11:49.930
Have you been satisfied
with Wine Library's

00:11:49.930 --> 00:11:52.763
performance since leaving
to focus on VaynerMedia?"

00:11:54.852 --> 00:11:56.059
- Andrew, this is a great question.

00:11:56.059 --> 00:11:57.731
I mean, I always say
everything stems from the top,

00:11:57.731 --> 00:12:00.704
and so I'm trying to
think about how I wanna

00:12:00.704 --> 00:12:04.071
answer this question,
meaning A.J. is ridiculously

00:12:04.071 --> 00:12:05.139
capable.

00:12:05.139 --> 00:12:07.669
I don't think the
company would do as well,

00:12:07.669 --> 00:12:10.339
mainly because he just had his big brother

00:12:10.339 --> 00:12:12.569
and mentor die, and so even though he's

00:12:12.569 --> 00:12:14.541
capable I would assume that he would be

00:12:14.541 --> 00:12:15.494
pretty torn up.

00:12:15.494 --> 00:12:16.725
He better be.

00:12:16.725 --> 00:12:19.256
I think that he would struggle with that,

00:12:19.256 --> 00:12:21.740
and I don't think he loves
client services enough

00:12:21.740 --> 00:12:24.502
to persevere, and he'd be like,
what is it all worth anyway?

00:12:24.502 --> 00:12:25.548
Who cares?

00:12:25.548 --> 00:12:29.031
On the flip side, there's
an interesting thing.

00:12:29.031 --> 00:12:31.259
Believe it or not, this is a weird thing.

00:12:31.259 --> 00:12:34.232
Though A.J. is hands down the most capable

00:12:34.232 --> 00:12:35.926
person to be the CEO of VaynerMedia,

00:12:35.926 --> 00:12:38.225
I could almost see him
not wanting to do it,

00:12:38.225 --> 00:12:40.802
and I could almost see so many people here

00:12:40.802 --> 00:12:42.080
internally saying, no we have to continue

00:12:42.080 --> 00:12:43.658
the hustle and so, it'd be interesting.

00:12:43.658 --> 00:12:45.423
I think we built a very
interesting culture here.

00:12:45.423 --> 00:12:50.067
Similarly, Brandon runs
Wine Library with my dad,

00:12:50.067 --> 00:12:52.482
and Bobby and Justin, it's all family.

00:12:52.482 --> 00:12:55.175
My best friend, my brother
in law, my cousin, my dad.

00:12:57.175 --> 00:12:59.564
My ego made me think that
Wine Library would hurt

00:12:59.564 --> 00:13:02.815
more than it did without me there.

00:13:02.815 --> 00:13:06.204
To answer your question, I am
happy with how Wine Library

00:13:06.204 --> 00:13:07.736
has performed with me not there.

00:13:07.736 --> 00:13:10.036
That being said, do I think it
could be way way, way better?

00:13:10.036 --> 00:13:11.683
Of course, I mean I think I'm great.

00:13:11.683 --> 00:13:15.582
Do I think the businesses
are better off without me

00:13:15.582 --> 00:13:17.034
than with me?
Absolutely not.

00:13:17.034 --> 00:13:20.133
Are they in places where they
won't go out of business?

00:13:20.133 --> 00:13:21.596
Absolutely.

00:13:21.596 --> 00:13:23.151
Are they in places where they have no

00:13:23.151 --> 00:13:25.520
prayer of the hyper growth that I create

00:13:25.520 --> 00:13:26.703
when I'm the operator?

00:13:26.703 --> 00:13:27.911
That's for damn sure.

00:13:27.911 --> 00:13:30.652
The biggest thing that
I create is the ability

00:13:30.652 --> 00:13:34.738
to grow big businesses fast as shit.

00:13:34.738 --> 00:13:38.151
That's gonna end up being my
legacy if I do it one more time

00:13:38.151 --> 00:13:40.171
and I'm not on business number two

00:13:40.171 --> 00:13:45.171
that I've taken in a 36 month
period with no cash infusion

00:13:45.419 --> 00:13:46.649
to very big heights.

00:13:46.649 --> 00:13:50.922
That is a very difficult
task in a cash flow basis.

00:13:50.922 --> 00:13:53.708
The companies that grow big on funding,

00:13:53.708 --> 00:13:55.100
that make sense.

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:57.702
The Ubers, and that
company is way better than

00:13:57.702 --> 00:13:59.141
what I've executed, but still when you

00:13:59.141 --> 00:14:00.674
have hundreds of millions
of dollars of funding,

00:14:00.674 --> 00:14:02.832
the speed is what I'm talking about.

00:14:02.832 --> 00:14:03.785
Forget about the business.

00:14:03.785 --> 00:14:05.759
Well in a non-funded business, to be able

00:14:05.759 --> 00:14:08.173
to build that speed,
that takes an incredible

00:14:08.173 --> 00:14:10.658
game of chicken, because
you're playing cash flow

00:14:10.658 --> 00:14:12.376
versus growth.

00:14:12.376 --> 00:14:13.583
Being able to afford.

00:14:13.583 --> 00:14:15.254
You know how proud I am that we've

00:14:15.254 --> 00:14:17.322
never had lay offs
because we lost a client?

00:14:17.322 --> 00:14:19.132
That is unheard of in agency world,

00:14:19.132 --> 00:14:21.130
and it's triple unheard of for the fastest

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:22.941
growing agency of all time in people.

00:14:22.941 --> 00:14:25.541
I'm proud.

00:14:25.541 --> 00:14:27.538
That is what I'm uniquely great at.

00:14:27.538 --> 00:14:30.602
They won't grow as fast,

00:14:30.602 --> 00:14:33.226
but there's enormous talent around me

00:14:33.226 --> 00:14:35.409
that is able to do their thing.

00:14:35.409 --> 00:14:37.383
That being said, I'm so much,

00:14:37.383 --> 00:14:41.261
not only the executional leader
of my friends and families

00:14:41.261 --> 00:14:43.233
and business, I think
I'm the emotional leader

00:14:43.233 --> 00:14:44.929
with a lot of them too.

00:14:44.929 --> 00:14:47.042
I would think that they
would really struggle

00:14:47.042 --> 00:14:50.850
with my absence, and would
crumble into a little hole.

00:14:50.850 --> 00:14:52.870
I'm just kidding.

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:54.699
I think they would struggle with that.

00:14:56.608 --> 00:14:57.625
Cool.

